  "cards": [
    { "dot": "violet", "title": "The organs (from the model's own config, not the repo)", "items": [
      "28 blocks; each: RMSNorm, attention, RMSNorm, feed-forward, both adding into the residual stream",
      "Grouped attention: 16 query heads share 8 key-value heads, head size 128",
      "Residual width 1024 equals the shipped vector's width, so every layer's state already lives in the map's space",
      "Pooling keeps the last token only (1_Pooling/config.json: pooling_mode_lasttoken); the final norm reads the residual stream after block 28",
      "Documents embed plain; queries get the instruction prefix 'Instruct: Given a web search query...'"
    ] },
    { "dot": "rose", "title": "The dissections", "items": [
      "D1, the shipped vector's coordinates: is the shared lean a few loud coordinates or spread over many? Zero model runs",
      "D2, the residual stream across depth: where is the cone born, where do topics separate, does any layer beat production on the gate",
      "D3, the summarizing heads: which words the last position draws from in the final blocks, then one head switched off",
      "Specimen for all three: Welch Labs, The moment we stopped understanding AI [AlexNet], 477 tokens, held since section 42"
    ] },
    { "dot": "emerald", "title": "Verified against the live store, 2026-10-31", "items": [
      "The cone: mean pair cosine 0.259, mean vector length 0.51, every note at cosine 0.51 to one shared direction (811 tagged notes; section 12 said the same on 493)",
      "A random pair's plane retains about 7.5x the chance length raw, 2.1x centred (section 15's single pair: 8.4x)",
      "70 of 84 scorable tags cohere raw, all 84 centred (section 10: 58 of 69, 69 of 69)",
      "The gate passed: hit@1 0.712, hit@5 0.897, hit@10 0.936, within tolerance of the 2026-07-26 stamp"
    ] },
    { "dot": "amber", "title": "What the repo never does", "items": [
      "No centring anywhere on the search path; Chroma compares raw cosine",
      "Never requests hidden states; output_hidden_states appears nowhere in ytk/ or scripts/",
      "Section 18's features came from Gemma Scope, another model; this encoder's interior is unopened"
    ] }
